NesPrgRom:1A7CB:ObjHandler_Tank_5F_Gray_Hopper_6HP_Init:ObjType $5F — Gray Hopper (6 HP), init. One-frame setup for the hopping enemy.
NesPrgRom:1A7CE:_ObjHandler_Tank_5F_Gray_Hopper_6HP_Init__Update__
NesPrgRom:1A7D0::Init the enemy from descriptor $05.
NesPrgRom:1A7D5::LoadedObj_Scratch is the base hop speed.  Set this to $30.
NesPrgRom:1A7D7::The next few lines set up the Facing field, but these values are overwritten before ever being used.\nAnd, unlike the attack phase, this choses to face AWAY from the player.
NesPrgRom:1A7DC::player is to the LEFT so set heading $C8 (11.25° CW from UP) which is AWAY from the player
NesPrgRom:1A7E1:_ObjHandler_Tank_5F_GrayHopper6HP_Init__Heading_PlayerRight:player is to the RIGHT so set heading to $B8 = $C0 (11.25° tilted CCW from UP) which, again, is AWAY from the player.
NesPrgRom:1A7E3:_ObjHandler_Tank_5F_GrayHopper6HP_Init__StoreFacing:commit the heading, then zero Velocity X/Y and the wind-up timer LoadedObj_AnimFrame
NesPrgRom:1A7ED:_ObjHandler_Tank_5F_Gray_Hopper_6HP_Init__Done
NesPrgRom:1A7EE:ObjHandler_Tank_60_Gray_Hopper_6HP_Attacking:ObjType $60 — Gray Hopper (6 HP), active: the hopping/attack half of the enemy. It falls under gravity; on each floor landing it either settles into the walking state $61 or aims a fresh, near-vertical hop at the player, and either way it then sits out a 10-frame wind-up on the ground before the stored hop velocity carries it up — so it bounds across the ground toward the player in bursts.
NesPrgRom:1A7F1:_ObjHandler_Tank_60_Gray_Hopper_6HP_Attacking__Update__:$42 = $80 / $43 = $C0: terrain-collision half-extents (16×24 box) — then gate on the wind-up timer $51
NesPrgRom:1A7FB::If LoadedObj_AnimFrame (wind-up) is at 0, then proceed to ground check.
NesPrgRom:1A7FD::otherwise, decrement LoadedObj_AnimFrame (wind-up).
NesPrgRom:1A802:_ObjHandler_Tank_60_GrayHopper6HP_Attacking__OnWindUpExpired:wind-up over: take one ballistic step (Obj_GravityMoveBounce_Double with gravity $04, which also reflects and damps the velocity on contact) and test bit 6 of the wall flags it returns — a vertical, i.e. floor-or-ceiling, contact. Clear means still airborne, so just draw.
NesPrgRom:1A80B::Handle vertical contact.  Obj_GravityMoveBounce_Double reflects LoadedObj's Velocity_Y on the hit so,\na negative value (pointing up) implies landing\na positive value implies a ceiling bonk.
NesPrgRom:1A80F::On Landed:\nSet the 10-frame wind-up (AnimFrame)
NesPrgRom:1A813::then spin Step_RNG to choose whicn state to transition to.
NesPrgRom:1A816::if either the Carry Flag is unset or if Global_FrameCounter is negative, then carry on with the attack.
NesPrgRom:1A81C::Otherwise, transition to the patrolling state.
NesPrgRom:1A821:_ObjHandler_Tank_60_GrayHopper6HP_Attacking__Jump:hop: play sound $29, then aim. The delta is the X distance (LoadedObj__Get_DeltaToPlayer_X = player.X − obj.X), not a Y distance — negative means the player is to the LEFT.
NesPrgRom:1A830:_ObjHandler_Tank_60_GrayHopper6HP_Attacking__Heading_PlayerLeft:player to the LEFT → heading $B8 = $C0 − $08, tilted 11.25° left of straight up (the $C8 above is the mirror, for a player to the right). This is the correctly-aimed pair; the Init at $A7DC/$A7E1 assigns the same two constants the other way round.
NesPrgRom:1A832:_ObjHandler_Tank_60_GrayHopper6HP_Attacking__Launch:launch: commit the heading to $47 and pass the speed magnitude $52 + (Step_RNG & $0F) = $30..$3F to Obj_AngleToVelocity in Y. This is a velocity computation, not a child spawn — $E1BD resolves heading+speed into $4C/$4D through Trig_QuarterSineTable.\nBecause $B8/$C8 sit only $08 either side of straight up, the components come out about 4:1 in favour of the vertical: |cos| = 25 and |sin| = 125 out of the table's $7F peak, scaled by the speed and shifted down 8, giving $4D ≈ −23..−30 (upward) against $4C ≈ ±4..±6. So it leaps almost straight up and only drifts onto the player.
NesPrgRom:1A840:_ObjHandler_Tank_60_GrayHopper6HP_Attacking__Render__:+0 (fade/freeze) entry, and the tail every other path falls into: $40/$41 give ScreenPos_Compute the box's FULL extent — $10 wide by $18 tall, a 16x24 box, which that routine halves itself. It returns $00 on-screen; anything else means the hopper has scrolled away, so park the slot via Obj_StashTypeSetState02.
NesPrgRom:1A850:_ObjHandler_Tank_60_GrayHopper6HP_Attacking__Damage:on-screen: run the shared damage check against descriptor $05. A non-zero return means this hit killed it — tail-call TankEnemy_Defeat, which does the per-slot bookkeeping and falls into the drop spawner.
NesPrgRom:1A85A:_ObjHandler_Tank_60_GrayHopper6HP_Attacking__Render:still alive: $44 = sprite palette 1, plus the horizontal-flip bit when the X velocity $4C is non-negative (Obj_SetAttrFlipX derives the flip from $4C, NOT from the heading $47). Then pick the pose from the wind-up timer.
NesPrgRom:1A863::$51 ≠ 0 — on the ground, winding up → metasprite $02, the crouched pose with the leg planted
NesPrgRom:1A868:_ObjHandler_Tank_60_GrayHopper6HP_Attacking__TileIdle:$51 = 0 — airborne (or free-falling) → metasprite $03, the tucked pose
NesPrgRom:1A86A:_ObjHandler_Tank_60_GrayHopper6HP_Attacking__SetTile:tail-call MetaSprite_Render ($F011) with the chosen metasprite id in A
