NesPrgRom:1AFFC:ObjHandler_Tank_76_Shooter_Init:(alpha: not fully human-verified / pending re-verification) ObjType $76 — Shooter (Thing $10, "Gray Shooter"), init. Launches the Shooter on a random straight line: a heading drawn from the RNG and a fixed speed, with its gun already loaded. Every Shooter therefore starts drifting in a different direction, and it is the Main handler's terrain bouncing that turns that into the circling patrol the player sees. TankEnemy_Init advances it to ObjType $77, so this runs for exactly one frame. Dual-entry: the +0 (fade/freeze) entry lands on the body's own RTS — this Init draws nothing. See docs/entities/tank/76-77_shooter.md
NesPrgRom:1AFFF:_ObjHandler_Tank_76_Shooter_Init__Update__:Normal-play body — pick a random heading and launch  [+3 body entry]\nenemy descriptor $10: HP 16, and a $80/256 (50%) chance of a Health-x1 ($2C) drop. TankEnemy_Init also does INC $46, so the next frame runs ObjType $77
NesPrgRom:1B004::$47 is the heading angle (0–255 = full circle), not a state byte — seed it straight from the RNG
NesPrgRom:1B009::speed $14, converted with the heading into the velocity pair $4C/$4D. This is the only place the Shooter's velocity is set; nothing steers it afterwards
NesPrgRom:1B00E::gun ready — no recoil to work off
NesPrgRom:1B012:_ObjHandler_Tank_76_Shooter_Init__Done:Init body terminal RTS; the +0 (render) entry JMPs here — this Init draws nothing.
NesPrgRom:1B013:ObjHandler_Tank_77_Shooter_Main:(alpha: not fully human-verified / pending re-verification) ObjType $77 — Shooter (Thing $10), active. A free-drifting enemy that bounces off terrain and shoots Small Red shots at the player, but only while its drift already carries it toward them and only at a player level with or below it — so it never fires backwards or upwards, and spends its time circling until the geometry lines up. Each shot costs a 16-frame recoil during which it holds a distinct pose and cannot fire again. HP 16; on death it explodes and may drop a Health-x1 pickup. Dual-entry: in normal play ($15 == 0) the object loop enters at +3 and runs the whole body; while a fade or freeze is up ($15 != 0) it enters at +0, which skips straight to the hit/render tail. See docs/entities/tank/76-77_shooter.md\n+0 (fade/freeze) entry: skip all logic, straight to the shared hit/render tail
NesPrgRom:1B016:_ObjHandler_Tank_77_Shooter_Main__Update__:Normal-play body — drift, then decide whether to fire  [+3 body entry]\n$42/$43 = $80: terrain-collision half-extents for the move below
NesPrgRom:1B01E::advance by velocity and bounce off walls (reflects $4C on a horizontal wall, $4D on a vertical one)
NesPrgRom:1B021::fire cooldown $52 — zero means free to fire
NesPrgRom:1B025::still cooling down: tick it and hold the recoil pose ($50 = 0)
NesPrgRom:1B02E:_ObjHandler_Tank_77_Shooter_Main__FireCheck:Fire gate — both aim conditions must hold, else fall through unfired\nsigned X-distance to player EOR X-velocity sign: negative = drifting AWAY, so hold fire
NesPrgRom:1B035::signed Y-distance: negative = player is above, so hold fire (it only shoots level or downward)
NesPrgRom:1B03A::child to spawn = ObjType $3C (Small Red shot)
NesPrgRom:1B03E::rate-limited spawn — throttles internally on the frame counter and RNG; Z = no shot this frame
NesPrgRom:1B043::shot away: start the 16-frame recoil cooldown
NesPrgRom:1B047:_ObjHandler_Tank_77_Shooter_Main__SetActive:Searching pose ($50 = 1) — reached whether or not a shot went out
NesPrgRom:1B04B:_ObjHandler_Tank_77_Shooter_Main__Render__:Shared hit/render tail — also the +0 (fade/freeze) entry\n$40/$41 = $10: 16×16 hitbox
NesPrgRom:1B053::screen position + overlap against the player's shots
NesPrgRom:1B058::off-screen: despawn
NesPrgRom:1B05B:_ObjHandler_Tank_77_Shooter_Main__Damage:Apply any hit, and die if it emptied the HP\nenemy descriptor $10 (HP 16)
NesPrgRom:1B062::killed: explosion, and maybe a Health-x1 drop
NesPrgRom:1B065:_ObjHandler_Tank_77_Shooter_Main__Render:Draw the sprite — pose follows the cooldown, facing follows the drift\nOAM attr = sprite sub-palette 1, H-flipped by the sign of $4C
NesPrgRom:1B06A::pose select: $50 non-zero (searching) keeps metasprite $6C…
NesPrgRom:1B070::…$50 == 0 (recoiling) bumps it to $6D
NesPrgRom:1B071:_ObjHandler_Tank_77_Shooter_Main__TileBase:Tail-call the metasprite renderer with the chosen id
