NesPrgRom:1D331::ASL doubles XVel before the add — this is the actual ×2 in "double speed".
NesPrgRom:1D337::Retrieve the sign-extension byte from the stack to carry into the x-metatile value.
NesPrgRom:1D33F::Update the TileIndex accordingly.
NesPrgRom:1D349:Apply_Double_Velocity_Y:Apply DOUBLE the LoadedObject's Y velocity to its position, adjusting tilemap index $4E by 16×row (row stride $11) and keeping $4B in 0-$7F. Dispatch $C042; Y half of Apply_Double_Velocity_XY.
NesPrgRom:1D351:_Apply_Double_Velocity_Y__PushSign:PHA the sign-extension byte ($00 or $FF) then add 2×YVel
NesPrgRom:1D374:L_D374
NesPrgRom:1D37A:L_D37A
NesPrgRom:1D37D:H_Collision_Check:X-axis terrain collision check and response — the horizontal mirror of V_Collision_Check.\nTests the level tiles the active object's collision box overlaps and, on a solid hit, snaps\nthe object flush against the blocking tile's edge. Reached through MoveX_WithCollision\n($D37A) and Collision_Checks ($D374); dispatch slot $C015.\nIn: LoadedObj_CollisionBox_HalfWidth/_HalfHeight (the box, centred on the object),\nLoadedObj_Position_X_Lo/_Y_Lo, LoadedObj_TileIndex. Out: Z=1 clear / Z=0 blocked, and on a\nhit LoadedObj_Position_X_Lo is rewritten so the box edge sits exactly on the tile boundary.\nThe X axis resolves on the exact edge; the Y axis it tests as a cross-check tolerates ~2 px\nof overlap before it counts, which is what stops an object catching on tile corners.\nSee docs/misc/terrain-collision.md
NesPrgRom:1D387:_H_Collision_Check__CheckRight:left edge clear → test the right edge (JSR _H_Collision_Check__TileRight); on hit snap $48 = -$42
NesPrgRom:1D393:_H_Collision_Check__Exit:RTS
NesPrgRom:1D394:_H_Collision_Check__TileRight:compute tile index for X pos + $42 (right edge); if overflow step to next column, then read/classify the tile
NesPrgRom:1D3A3:_H_Collision_Check__TileLeft:compute tile index for X pos vs $42 (left edge); if underflow step to prior column, then read/classify the tile
NesPrgRom:1D3A9::branch if LoadedObj's X_Lo (fixed4.4) >= the collision box's HalfWidth.\nThis means we can use LoadedObj's TileIndex as is.
NesPrgRom:1D3AB::Otherwise, decrement TileIndex (so we check one tile to the left)
NesPrgRom:1D3AC:_H_Collision_Check__ReadTile:Load tile flags into A.  Also check the bottom Y edge ($4A + $43, +$11 row)
NesPrgRom:1D3AF::Bit 7 (negative) means a solid tile was found.  Skip to Exit tail.
NesPrgRom:1D3B1::Otherwise, do the cross-axis checks
NesPrgRom:1D3C6:_H_Collision_Check__CheckTop:check the top Y edge ($4A - $43, -$11 row); solid → collision
NesPrgRom:1D3DB:_H_Collision_Check__NoCollide:all tiles clear → LDA #$00 (Z=1 no collision); RTS
NesPrgRom:1D3DE:L_D3DE
NesPrgRom:1D3E1:V_Collision_Check:Y-axis terrain collision check and response — the vertical mirror of H_Collision_Check.\nTests the level tiles the active object's collision box overlaps and, on a solid hit, snaps\nthe object flush against the blocking tile's edge — this is what makes an object land on a\nfloor or stop under a ceiling. Reached through MoveY_WithCollision ($D3DE) and\nCollision_Checks ($D374); dispatch slot $C018.\nIn: LoadedObj_CollisionBox_HalfHeight/_HalfWidth (the box, centred on the object),\nLoadedObj_Position_Y_Lo/_X_Lo, LoadedObj_TileIndex. Out: Z=1 clear / Z=0 blocked, and on a\nhit LoadedObj_Position_Y_Lo is rewritten so the box edge sits exactly on the tile boundary.\nSee docs/misc/terrain-collision.md\ncheck the tile above ($D40B); if solid, snap the position so the box top rests on it
NesPrgRom:1D3E4::tile above solid: LDA $43 → STA $4A (snap position to tile edge); RTS
NesPrgRom:1D3EB:_V_Collision_Check__CheckBelow:check tile below ($D3F8); if solid: snap ObjYFrac = -$43 (push up to tile bottom)
NesPrgRom:1D3EE::tile below solid: 0-$43 → $4A; RTS
NesPrgRom:1D3F8:_V_Collision_Check__TileBelow:compute tile index for position + $43 (bottom edge); if overflow: step to next tile row
NesPrgRom:1D3FF::Branch if A is 0
NesPrgRom:1D401::Branch if Y_Lo and HalfHeight didn't overflow
NesPrgRom:1D403::otherwise, adjust TileIndex (to one row lower) before testing tile
NesPrgRom:1D40B:_V_Collision_Check__TileAbove:compute tile index for position vs $43 (top edge); if BCS: step to prior tile row
NesPrgRom:1D418:_V_Collision_Check__ReadTile:Use TileIndex (X) to load the target tile's flags.\nbit 7 being set means the tile is solid.  In this case, we use the escape hatch via BMI.\nOtherwise, check left/right X edge tiles
NesPrgRom:1D41D:_V_Collision_Check__CheckRight:RIGHT-edge X cross-check: Position_X_Lo + the half-width. If it carries, the right edge has spilled into the next column, so test that tile too — but only once the spill reaches $20 (2 px); a shallower overlap is ignored, which is what keeps an object from catching on a tile corner.
NesPrgRom:1D42F:_V_Collision_Check__CheckLeft:LEFT-edge X cross-check: Position_X_Lo − the half-width. If it borrows, the left edge has crossed into the previous column, so test that tile too — subject to the same 2 px ($E0) corner tolerance as the right edge above.
NesPrgRom:1D440:_V_Collision_Check__NoCollide:all tiles clear; Z=1 → signals no collision to caller
NesPrgRom:1D442:_V_Collision_Check__Exit:RTS (Z=0 from a solid-tile BMI = collision; Z=1 = clear)
