NesPrgRom:1DF84:Obj_MoveBounce_Double:Double-speed variant of Obj_MoveBounce: advance via Obj_MoveAndCollide_Double and reflect velocity on collisions.\nFlags:\n  bit7 (side wall) negates XVel $4C,\n  bit6 (floor/ceiling) negates YVel $4D. \n\nOutput:\n A = wall flags\n TerrainCollisionFlags = wall flags
NesPrgRom:1DF87::Branch on positive, means branch when bit 7 is 0.  This means no x-collision.
NesPrgRom:1DF89::On negative, however, handle X-bounce.\nSet Accumulator to 0, then subtract X-Velocity to get the mirrored value
NesPrgRom:1DF8E::Save mirrored X-Velocity
NesPrgRom:1DF93:_Obj_MoveBounce_Double__CheckVertical:Probe bit6 (floor/ceiling) set → negate YVel $4D.
NesPrgRom:1DF96::Handle Y-bounce\nSet Accumulator to 0, then subtract Y-Velocity to get the mirrored value
NesPrgRom:1DF9B::Save mirrored X-Velocity
NesPrgRom:1DF9D:_Obj_MoveBounce_Double__Return:Return the wall flags ($9A).
NesPrgRom:1DFA0:Obj_GravityMoveBounce_Double:Adds gravity (A) to LoadedObj's Velocity_Y then moves at double speed with wall reflection. Dampens the bounce to 1/4 on a floor/ceiling hit, and clamps both velocities to ±$28.\n\nInput:\n  A = Gravity\n\nOutput:\n  A = Wall flags\n    bit 7 for horizontal collisions\n    bit 6 for vertical collisions\n  \n  LoadedObj's Velocity_Y = previous velocity with gravity applied and reflected if that movement resulted in a collision with a floor or ceiling.
NesPrgRom:1DFA6::This always branches.
NesPrgRom:1DFA8::dead
NesPrgRom:1DFA9::dead
NesPrgRom:1DFAC:_Obj_GravityMoveBounce_Double__ApplyGravity:Gravity is popped from stack and added to the LoadedObj's Y velocity.\nThe BVS guard skips the store on signed overflow.
NesPrgRom:1DFB4:_Obj_GravityMoveBounce_Double__Move:Double move+bounce; floor/ceiling hit (bit6) → damp YVel to 1/4 ($40/256).
NesPrgRom:1DFC0:_Obj_GravityMoveBounce_Double__ClampSpeed:Clamp LoadedObj's velocities
NesPrgRom:1DFC4::The previous two lines prepare a call into Speed_Limit_Sub.\n\nA = Clamp value ($28)\nX = Value to be clamped.  In this case, LoadedObj's Velocity_Y ($4D)\n\nonce prepped, call the sub.
NesPrgRom:1DFCB::Repeat for LoadedObj's Velocity_X ($4C)
NesPrgRom:1DFCE::Return TerrainCollisionFlags in A
