NesPrgRom:1E182:ScaleByUnsignedFrac:Unsigned fractional scale — multiply MulDiv_Op1 by the unsigned fraction in MulDiv_Op2. The unsigned half of ScaleBySignedFrac.\n\nInput:\n  MulDiv_Op1 = value to scale, in any fixed-point format\n  MulDiv_Op2 = scale, as fixed08 (0.ffffffff)\n\nOutput:\n  A          = MulDiv_Op1 x MulDiv_Op2, in Op1's own format\n  MulDiv_Op1 = the same value (the result is written back over the input)
NesPrgRom:1E184::A is the running total; the X above counts the 8 shift/add steps, one per bit of MulDiv_Op1.
NesPrgRom:1E186:_ScaleByUnsignedFrac__Loop:Shift the next multiplier bit out of MulDiv_Op1; when set, add the (progressively halved) multiplicand MulDiv_Op2.
NesPrgRom:1E18D:_ScaleByUnsignedFrac__Next:Halve MulDiv_Op2 — halving the multiplicand each step is what makes the routine lossy, and what leaves the final LSR to supply the last division by 2.
NesPrgRom:1E196:ScaleBySignedFrac:Signed fractional scale — A = A x Y / 128, with A's sign preserved.\n\nInput:\n  A = signed byte, in any fixed-point format\n  Y = unsigned byte, in any fixed-point format\n\nOutput:\n  A = A x Y / 128, A's sign preserved. Approximate and never over-estimated — the magnitude comes from ScaleByUnsignedFrac ($E182), which is low by 0..3. |result| must be < $80, that routine's precondition.
NesPrgRom:1E198::ASL A does double duty:\n\n1. it shifts the sign bit into Carry (Carry set for negative)\n2. it doubles A, rescaling it from sfixed17 (s.fffffff) to the fixed08 (0.ffffffff) that ScaleByUnsignedFrac expects.\n\nFor A < 0 the doubled value is still two's complement here (and for |A| > $40 it no longer\neven has bit 7 set); the fixed08 magnitude only appears after the negate below.
NesPrgRom:1E199::For non-negative A values, jump to positive handler.
NesPrgRom:1E19B::For negative A values,\n\nnegate the doubled value,
NesPrgRom:1E1A2::scale,
NesPrgRom:1E1A5::and negate the product back.
NesPrgRom:1E1AB:_ScaleBySignedFrac__Positive:A >= 0: the doubled value needs no sign fixup — multiply and return.
NesPrgRom:1E1B1:L_E1B1
NesPrgRom:1E1B7:L_E1B7
NesPrgRom:1E1BD:Obj_AngleToVelocity:Convert LoadedObj's Facing (heading) to a scaled Velocity vector\n\nInput:\n  LoadedObj.Facing = angle as 0-255 spanning a full circle\n  Y = scale factor\n\nOutput:\n  LoadedObj.Velocity_X = cos(LoadedObj.Facing) x scale\n  LoadedObj.Velocity_Y = sin(LoadedObj.Facing) x scale
NesPrgRom:1E1BF::Look up cos(A)
NesPrgRom:1E1C2::Scale by Y
NesPrgRom:1E1C5::Save into LoadedObj.Velocity_X
