NesPrgRom:1E697:OAM_Copy_To_PPU:Uploads the $0200 sprite page to PPU OAM. \nIf the mode flag OAM_Flag__HARDCODED_00 is 0, triggers a full 256-byte sprite DMA via $4014 (OAMADDR reset to 0); \notherwise copies 64 bytes/frame manually through OAMDATA ($2004), advancing the quarter index $F0 ($00/$40/$80/$C0) so the page uploads over four frames.
NesPrgRom:1E6A7:_DEAD_OAM_Copy_To_PPU__Manually:Dead in the shipped US ROM — the alternate manual OAM upload path (stream $0200 → OAM data port $2004), reached only when OAM_Flag__HARDCODED_00 ($E6BE) ≠ 0, which it never is; the $4014 sprite-DMA fall-through above is what actually runs.
NesPrgRom:1E6B1:_DEAD_OAM_Copy_To_PPU__ManualLoop:Copy 64 bytes $0200+X → OAM data port ($2004).
NesPrgRom:1E6BE:OAM_Flag__HARDCODED_00:Single ROM byte, $00 in the shipped ROM - a build-time switch read (never written) by OAM_Copy_To_PPU ($E697) and OAM_BlitFromStaging ($EC77). Both do LDA OAM_Flag__HARDCODED_00 / BNE, so with $00 the branch never fires: OAM always goes out via $4014 sprite DMA (not the manual copy path), and the staging blit always uses NmiFrameFlag ($11) bit 0 frame parity to alternate slot direction rather than a forced direction. Patching this byte non-zero enables the two dead alternate paths.
