NesPrgRom:1EB14:Speed_Limit_Sub:Clamps the signed velocity ZP[$00+X] into [-A, +A]\n\nInput:\n  X = the ZP index\n  A = the positive speed limit
NesPrgRom:1EB18::When Velocity is non-negative:\n\nCompare limit A against Velocity
NesPrgRom:1EB1A::if A >= Velocity, return without change.
NesPrgRom:1EB1C::otherwise (clamping is required since Velocity > A), clamp ZP[$00+X] to A
NesPrgRom:1EB1F:_Speed_Limit_Sub__Negative:When Velocity is negative:\n\nnegate A via two's complement → -A for comparison
NesPrgRom:1EB24::Compare limit -A against negative velocity
NesPrgRom:1EB26::if -A < Velocity, return without change.
NesPrgRom:1EB28::otherwise (clamping is probably required since Velocity <= -A), clamp ZP[$00+X] to A
NesPrgRom:1EB2A:_Speed_Limit_Sub__Return:RTS (velocity within limit).
