NesInternalRam:0046:LoadedObj__Type:Entity type / ObjType. 0 = empty (inactive slot); 1 = reserved; 2 = tombstoned; any other value dispatches to an AI handler.
NesInternalRam:0047:LoadedObj__Facing:Direction byte (ObjType-defined: 8-bit heading angle / 2-bit direction index / facing bit-flags).
NesInternalRam:0048:LoadedObj__Position_X_Lo:The lower 8-bits of the Signed 16-bit Fixed Point position (swww wwww WWWW.FFFF) representing the object's X-position.
NesInternalRam:0049:LoadedObj__Position_X_Hi:The upper 8-bits of the Signed 16-bit Fixed Point position (SWWW WWWW wwww.ffff) representing the object's X-position.
NesInternalRam:004A:LoadedObj__Position_Y_Lo:The lower 8-bits of the Signed 16-bit Fixed Point position (swww wwww WWWW.FFFF) representing the object's Y-position.
NesInternalRam:004B:LoadedObj__Position_Y_Hi:The upper 8-bits of the Signed 16-bit Fixed Point position (SWWW WWWW wwww.ffff) representing the object's Y-position.
NesInternalRam:004C:LoadedObj__Velocity_X:X velocity in px/frame (signed 4.4: swww.ffff).
NesInternalRam:004D:LoadedObj__Velocity_Y:Y velocity in px/frame (signed 4.4: swww.ffff).
NesInternalRam:004E:LoadedObj__TileIndex:(alpha: not fully human-verified / pending re-verification) Index of the tile this object currently occupies in the loaded tile-flag window LevelTileData ($0500) -- a COLLISION index, not a render/sprite tile id. Confirmed by its only dereferencing sites: $D2AB/$D2AD (LDX $4E / LDA $0500,X, the tile-flag read) and $CEC6/$CEC8 (LDX $4E / STA $0500,X, the write-back). The window is 17 tiles per row, which is why the movement helpers step it by +/-17 for a row change (_Apply_Velocity_Y__AdjTileIndex $D67B) and +/-1 for a column change.
NesInternalRam:004F:LoadedObj__ActiveFlag:(alpha: not fully human-verified / pending re-verification) Post-damage invincibility frames (drives the flashing damage animation).
NesInternalRam:0050:LoadedObj__Phase:(alpha: not fully human-verified / pending re-verification) State/phase byte -- which branch of the object's own state machine it is in (ObjType-defined): the player uses it as a physics sub-state (0 grounded, 1 jump/hit-recover, 2 crouch, 3 ladder, 4 walk); enemies use it as a behaviour phase -- e.g. the Jellyfish ($81) 0 = sinking / 1 = jetting, the Kamikaze Orb ($79) 0 = patrolling / 1 = charging, the Shooter ($77) as its recoil pose.
NesInternalRam:0051:LoadedObj__AnimFrame:(alpha: not fully human-verified / pending re-verification) Animation / timer counter.
NesInternalRam:0052:LoadedObj__Scratch:(alpha: not fully human-verified / pending re-verification) Type-specific scratch (slot byte 12).
NesInternalRam:0053:LoadedObj__Health:HP for this entity.
NesInternalRam:0056:ObjectSlot_Offset:Byte offset of the active slot
NesInternalRam:0057:ObjectSlot_Index:Index of the active slot
NesInternalRam:007C:PlayerContact__XPos:(alpha: not fully human-verified / pending re-verification) Screen X, posted by Sprite_Update ($D7A0) from WR_Context_Dependent_3E.
NesInternalRam:007D:PlayerContact__YPos:(alpha: not fully human-verified / pending re-verification) Screen Y, posted by Sprite_Update ($D7A0) from WR_Context_Dependent_3F.
NesInternalRam:007E:PlayerContact__Damage:(alpha: not fully human-verified / pending re-verification) Bit 7 = hit flag, bits 0-6 = damage magnitude. Sprite_Update posts (A & $7F) -- bit 7 is always cleared on post -- and returns the PREVIOUS byte, which is how the owner learns it was hit. An attacker stamps its own magnitude | $80 here (Enemy_Damage_Check_Sub $D6C8 / HitboxScan_LockOn $D71A / HitboxTest_LockOn $D75B). $7F posted means harmless: a scanner reads it as the damage TO ITSELF and $D69C skips on cmp #$7F, which is how touching Jason/Sophia costs an enemy nothing. See EnemyDesc::ContactDamage.
NesInternalRam:007F:Projectile1__XPos:(alpha: not fully human-verified / pending re-verification) Screen X, posted by Sprite_Update ($D7A0) from WR_Context_Dependent_3E.
