NesInternalRam:041B:Object_Slot_01__Health:HP for this entity.
NesInternalRam:041C:Object_Slot_02__Type:Entity type / ObjType. 0 = empty (inactive slot); 1 = reserved; 2 = tombstoned; any other value dispatches to an AI handler.
NesInternalRam:041D:Object_Slot_02__Facing:Direction byte (ObjType-defined: 8-bit heading angle / 2-bit direction index / facing bit-flags).
NesInternalRam:041E:Object_Slot_02__Position_X_Lo:The lower 8-bits of the Signed 16-bit Fixed Point position (swww wwww WWWW.FFFF) representing the object's X-position.
NesInternalRam:041F:Object_Slot_02__Position_X_Hi:The upper 8-bits of the Signed 16-bit Fixed Point position (SWWW WWWW wwww.ffff) representing the object's X-position.
NesInternalRam:0420:Object_Slot_02__Position_Y_Lo:The lower 8-bits of the Signed 16-bit Fixed Point position (swww wwww WWWW.FFFF) representing the object's Y-position.
NesInternalRam:0421:Object_Slot_02__Position_Y_Hi:The upper 8-bits of the Signed 16-bit Fixed Point position (SWWW WWWW wwww.ffff) representing the object's Y-position.
NesInternalRam:0422:Object_Slot_02__Velocity_X:X velocity in px/frame (signed 4.4: swww.ffff).
NesInternalRam:0423:Object_Slot_02__Velocity_Y:Y velocity in px/frame (signed 4.4: swww.ffff).
NesInternalRam:0424:Object_Slot_02__TileIndex:(alpha: not fully human-verified / pending re-verification) Index of the tile this object currently occupies in the loaded tile-flag window LevelTileData ($0500) -- a COLLISION index, not a render/sprite tile id. Confirmed by its only dereferencing sites: $D2AB/$D2AD (LDX $4E / LDA $0500,X, the tile-flag read) and $CEC6/$CEC8 (LDX $4E / STA $0500,X, the write-back). The window is 17 tiles per row, which is why the movement helpers step it by +/-17 for a row change (_Apply_Velocity_Y__AdjTileIndex $D67B) and +/-1 for a column change.
NesInternalRam:0425:Object_Slot_02__ActiveFlag:(alpha: not fully human-verified / pending re-verification) Post-damage invincibility frames (drives the flashing damage animation).
NesInternalRam:0426:Object_Slot_02__Phase:(alpha: not fully human-verified / pending re-verification) State/phase byte -- which branch of the object's own state machine it is in (ObjType-defined): the player uses it as a physics sub-state (0 grounded, 1 jump/hit-recover, 2 crouch, 3 ladder, 4 walk); enemies use it as a behaviour phase -- e.g. the Jellyfish ($81) 0 = sinking / 1 = jetting, the Kamikaze Orb ($79) 0 = patrolling / 1 = charging, the Shooter ($77) as its recoil pose.
NesInternalRam:0427:Object_Slot_02__AnimFrame:(alpha: not fully human-verified / pending re-verification) Animation / timer counter.
NesInternalRam:0428:Object_Slot_02__Scratch:(alpha: not fully human-verified / pending re-verification) Type-specific scratch (slot byte 12).
NesInternalRam:0429:Object_Slot_02__Health:HP for this entity.
